    <!-- THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT - a comment placed ABOVE
         <FlexiPage> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
         matching parent xml file" error.

         =====================================================================
         🔴 2026-08-26 - "ADVANCE STAGE" IS REPLACED BY NAMED PER-HOP BUTTONS ON THE DISPOSITION
         SIDE ONLY. USER DECISION: "we don't need a quick action named 'Advance Stage'; instead we
         need the NEXT STAGE NAME."
         =====================================================================

         THREE NEW ENTRIES, ONE PER HOP OF NDA_DISPOSITION_NEXT_STAGE, each labelled with the stage
         the click lands on: Move_to_Approved ("Approved", at Prepare), Move_to_Sent ("Sent", at
         Approved and at the legacy Not Sent) and Move_to_Signed ("Signed", at Sent). All three
         point at the SAME c/advanceRecordStage bundle the generic button uses - the target is
         derived server-side from the record's current status, per record type, so the label is a
         promise this file's visibility rules keep rather than anything the client sends.

         🔴 ACQUISITION IS UNCHANGED, AND THAT WAS THE CONSTRAINT, NOT A SIDE EFFECT. Both
         pre-existing Advance_Stage entries KEEP their criteria and each gains ONE more:
         {!Record.RecordType.DeveloperName} NE Disposition_NDA. On an Acquisition_NDA row that
         criterion is TRUE, so nothing an acquisition user sees moves. On a Master-typed row
         RecordType.DeveloperName reads BLANK and blank NE 'Disposition_NDA' is also TRUE, so the
         button FAILS OPEN there - the polarity code review forced on LOI_Record_Page's criterion 5
         (C2, 2026-08-21) for exactly this reason. The three NEW entries use the opposite operator,
         EQUAL Disposition_NDA, which fails CLOSED on Master; that is correct for them, because a
         disposition-only button must not appear on a row whose type nobody has set.

         ⚠ IT TAKES THE CRITERION ON *BOTH* Advance_Stage ENTRIES TO EMPTY THE BUTTON FROM A
         DISPOSITION ROW, NOT JUST THE DISPOSITION-GATED ONE. The Acquisition_Deal_Actions entry
         has always rendered on a disposition NDA for anyone holding that permission (this page and
         LOI_Record_Page both record it as an accepted cosmetic residual that "fails loudly" at the
         server). Left alone it would have gone on rendering "Advance Stage" beside the new named
         buttons.

         ⚠ THE DISPOSITION-GATED Advance_Stage ENTRY NOW HAS NO TRUE-CASE ON ANY ROW, AND IS
         DELIBERATELY RETAINED RATHER THAN DELETED. Its criterion 2 is Is_Decline_Allowed__c, whose
         formula is AND(RecordType.DeveloperName = "Disposition_NDA", ...), and its new criterion 4
         demands NE Disposition_NDA - a contradiction, so it renders nowhere. Deleting it is the
         tidier change and is NOT made here: this file's whole edit was scoped to "add a criterion,
         change nothing else", and a deletion is the kind of change that has emptied action bars in
         this repo before. Remove it as a separate, deliberate step if wanted.

         ⚠ Move_to_Sent APPEARS TWICE, ON PURPOSE. NDA_DISPOSITION_NEXT_STAGE maps BOTH
         'Approved' => 'Sent' and the legacy 'Not Sent' => 'Sent', and a flexipage booleanFilter
         has no OR the renderer honours (measured on this page's sibling: a parenthesised OR
         deploys, survives a retrieve and is ignored). Two valueListItems carrying the same <value>
         is the shape this page itself introduced. The two are mutually exclusive by construction -
         Status__c holds one value - so the button cannot render twice, which is a stronger
         guarantee than the two Advance_Stage entries ever had. 'Not Sent' is on NO record type
         since 2026-08-25 and a live aggregate that day measured ZERO rows carrying it; the entry
         exists to match the service map, which keeps that hop on purpose. Retire both together.

         🔴 THIS FILE'S OWN PARAGRAPH "WHY A NEW FORMULA FIELD RATHER THAN
         {!Record.RecordType.DeveloperName} DIRECTLY IN THE VISIBILITY RULE" (below) IS NOW STALE
         AND MUST NOT BE QUOTED AS A REASON NOT TO DO THIS. It says the construct is
         "REPO-ASSERTED AND UNMEASURED at the flexipage layer" and that "no flexipage in this repo
         has ever carried a bare {!Record.RecordType.*} criterion". Both were true when written on
         2026-08-21 and both were overtaken the SAME DAY: LOI_Record_Page's criterion 5 is exactly
         that construct, and it was validated by a four-probe check-only control against
         usman-dpeg. Probe B is the one that matters - a bogus field placed BEHIND the RecordType
         hop was rejected BY NAME, which proves the validator traversed the relationship and
         resolved the field rather than waving a string through. The formula-checkbox alternative
         was rejected here because it would mean THREE new formula fields plus FLS for each, and
         because Is_Disposition_NDA__c already exists but is granted only on the two disposition
         sets - a criterion reading a field the running user cannot read evaluates FALSE, which
         would have hidden the acquisition Advance Stage button from every acquisition persona.

         ⚠ STILL NOT PROVEN, AND NOT PROVABLE FROM A REPO: RENDERER BEHAVIOUR. Metadata validation
         exercises the metadata layer only. After deploying, a human must open (1) a disposition
         NDA at each of Prepare / Approved / Sent and confirm exactly ONE correctly-named button
         and NO "Advance Stage", (2) an acquisition NDA at Pending / Received / Signed and confirm
         "Advance Stage" is still there and none of the new buttons is, and (3) a Master-typed NDA
         if one can be made, confirming "Advance Stage" survives. Checking only direction (1) makes
         a rule the renderer ignores look identical to one that works.

         NO PERMISSION SET CHANGED. All six criteria in the new entries read either the
         Disposition_Deal_Actions custom permission (no FLS to be missing) or Status__c /
         RecordType, both already readable by DPEG_Disposition_Edit and DPEG_Disposition_View
         (NDA__c.Status__c measured present in both). Nothing new needs granting.

         🔴 AMENDED 2026-08-21 (buyer-to-broker-counterparty-change.md), LATER THE SAME DAY AS
         THE "THREE FIELDS ADDED" NOTE DIRECTLY BELOW. Record.Buyer__c is REMOVED from this page
         and replaced, in the same slot and under the same Is_Disposition_NDA__c visibility rule,
         by Record.Broker__c (identifier RecordBroker_cField, was RecordBuyer_cField). User
         decision: "we don't need buyer information, we just need broker contact for disposition
         offers and NDA" - DPEG communicates only with the appointed listing broker on the sale.
         NDA__c.Buyer__c itself is NOT deleted (additive-only rule; see the field's own comment)
         but is no longer reachable from this page. NDA__c.Materials_Released_Date__c is
         untouched - the timeline still uses it and it keeps its own visibility rule below.
         FLS for the new field ships in the same change: DPEG_Disposition_Edit gets read+edit,
         DPEG_Disposition_View gets read only, matching how Buyer__c was granted before it.

         THREE FIELDS ADDED 2026-08-21 (buyer activity timeline follow-up). Record.Disposition__c,
         Record.Buyer__c and Record.Materials_Released_Date__c were carrying no path to render
         anywhere on this page - the disposition NDA had no visible link back to its Disposition,
         and Buyer__c / Materials_Released_Date__c (deployed 2026-08-20 for the buyer activity
         timeline) had never been added to any page, so nobody could set either one. All three are
         disposition-module-only fields on a dual-module object (Acquisition_NDA / Disposition_NDA
         share NDA__c) and are meaningless on an acquisition NDA.

         🔴 GATED ON RECORD TYPE, NOT ON WHETHER Disposition__c IS POPULATED. An analyst opening a
         brand-new disposition NDA needs to SEE the blank Disposition lookup to fill it in;
         ISBLANK(Disposition__c) would hide the exact field that needs populating. See
         objects/NDA__c/fields/Is_Disposition_NDA__c.field-meta.xml for the full reasoning and why
         it is a new field rather than a reuse of Is_Decline_Allowed__c (that one additionally
         excludes Declined, which would wrongly hide these three fields on a declined NDA).

         WHY A NEW FORMULA FIELD RATHER THAN {!Record.RecordType.DeveloperName} DIRECTLY IN THE
         VISIBILITY RULE. LOI_Record_Page's 2026-08-14 amendment names that construct
         REPO-ASSERTED AND UNMEASURED at the flexipage layer - no flexipage in this repo has ever
         carried a bare {!Record.RecordType.*} criterion, and this repo has separately measured a
         DIFFERENT construct (a parenthesised OR) that deploys, survives a retrieve, and is then
         IGNORED BY THE RENDERER. The formula-checkbox shape, by contrast, is proven: it already
         gates the Mark Declined button on THIS SAME PAGE (Is_Decline_Allowed__c) and passed this
         org's check-only validation both there and in All_NDAs_Signed_Before_Progression. This
         change reuses the proven mechanism for three fields rather than risking the first
         flexipage-level test of the unproven one.

         🔴 THIS CHANGE INTENTIONALLY LEAVES Record.Opportunity__c UNGATED, EXACTLY AS FOUND. It
         carries no visibilityRule today and is visible on BOTH record types (Opportunity__c is
         blank on a disposition NDA, since that side is parented by Disposition__c instead - see
         Disposition__c's own field comment). Symmetric gating (hiding Opportunity__c on a
         disposition NDA the same way these three fields are hidden on an acquisition NDA) was
         NOT applied here - that changes existing, working behaviour on the acquisitions module and
         was flagged rather than changed, per instruction. RECOMMENDATION: gate it symmetrically
         with the same {!Record.Is_Disposition_NDA__c} EQUAL false test for visual consistency (an
         always-blank field on a disposition NDA is confusing whitespace, not a defect), but this is
         a user decision, not an assumed follow-on to this change.

         FLS IS LOAD-BEARING FOR ALL FOUR FIELDS REFERENCED BY THE NEW VISIBILITY RULES.
         Disposition__c, Buyer__c and Materials_Released_Date__c already carry read FLS in both
         DPEG_Disposition_View and DPEG_Disposition_Edit (verified against those files' current
         state, not assumed). Is_Disposition_NDA__c is a NEW field and its grant ships in the same
         change - see permissionsets/DPEG_Disposition_View.permissionset-meta.xml and
         DPEG_Disposition_Edit.permissionset-meta.xml. None of the four is granted on any
         acquisition permission set, matching this object's existing convention.

         PLACEMENT: Disposition__c sits immediately after Opportunity__c (both are the parent-link
         pair - one populated per record type). Buyer__c and Materials_Released_Date__c are
         appended at the tail of the same facet, after OneDrive_URL__c, following this repo's
         tail-append convention for later additions to an existing field run. uiBehavior is `none`
         (editable) on all three, matching every other business field in this facet - none of them
         is a derived/stamped field on this page. -->
